<title>JAPAN: Japan July copper imports up 17.4 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan July copper imports up 17.4 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined copper imports in July totalled 28,075 tonnes, up 17.4 percent from 23,909 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   July 96	  June 96	 July 95</p>
<p> Total	   28,075	   21,503	  23,909</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Chile	   10,493	    7,224	   6,522</p>
<p> U.S.	     4,076	    4,009	   4,082</p>
<p> Zambia	   4,459	    3,637	   5,005</p>
<p>Imports in the first seven months of 1996 were 220,462 tonnes, against 266,223 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
</text>
